    "description": "16+ years of Android development experience.\n\nAndroid related Skills:\nAndroid Studio, Android SDK, Kotlin, MVVM, Kotlin Multiplatform, Flutter, Java, Jetpack, Compose, Compose Multiplatform, Coroutines, Room database, Reactive Programming (Flows/RxJava), Dependency Injection (Koin, Dagger/Hilt), NDK/JNI, C++, Unit and UI testing (e.g. Espresso, Appium, Browserstack), Exoplayer, GraphQL, REST, Bluetooth/BLE, IntelliJ IDEA… plus more.\n\nI also have iOS Native experience.\n\nI extensively use Claude Code, Codex, Gemini/Antigravity, Grok, GitHub Copilot.\n\n30+ years of C/C++ development experience.\n\nOther Skills:\nC99, C11, C17, C23, C++98, C++03, C++11, C++14, C++17, C++20, C++23, Go Lang, NFC, please see skills below.\n\nNetworking, Sockets, Concurrency/Multi-Threading, OpenCV, FFmpeg, Code Coverage tools, Android and Java JNI/NDK, Embedded, Linux, IoT, Assembly Language, SPI, I2C, CAN bus, OBD-II, WIFI… plus more.\n\nIDEs:\nJetBrains CLion, Visual Studio, Microchip MPLAB, Android Studio, GoLand\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOther Important Experience:\nDocker, Wireshark, Git, GitHub, Jira, Confluence, Figma, Slack\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIndustries I have contracted in: \nAerospace/Marine, Mining/Fleet Management/Fleet Tracking, Defense/Homeland Security, Financial/Financial Engineering, Insurance, Real Estate, HealthCare/Medical Devices, Geographic Information Systems (GIS), eCommerce, Consumer Facing Apps to broadly name a few.\n\nClients, a partial list: \nContracted with: Boeing, Charles Schwab, Goodyear Tire and Rubber, NASA, Sandia National Lab, Los Alamos National Lab, Thermo Fisher Scientific, Jackson National Life, Skyhook Wireless, Agile Data Decisions LLC and Myia Labs, Davis Instruments, New York Public Library, Auddia and many others.",
